ws of his  famous father the movie follows Charlie  a troubled teen whose struggles land him  in rehab according to Nick however it  wasn't always destined to be a movie  originally beginning Life as a pilot  script for a half hour comedy series he  developed the concept while he himself  was staying at a rehabilitation clinic  and it eventually morphed into a script  for a movie with the help of his father  in fact the making of being Charlie  helped heal a rift between the real-life  Father and Son Duo Rob Reiner told ABC  News in 2015 over the course of making  the film our relationship definitely  changed it wasn't terrible or anything  but it got better because I then  understood a lot more of what he had  gone through and he understood a bit  more of what I had gone through arguably  David Lynch's defining film Mulholland  Drive is a dark drama about an aspiring  actress who befriends a young woman  suffering from Amnesia a masterpiece of  modern Cinema its mix of mystery crime  Noir abstract Dreamscape and genuine  Horror made it not just one of Lynch's  best but a film many consider flawless  no I Banda  it is all  fans of the film might be surprised to  learn it almost wasn't a movie at all as  Mulholland Drive was originally dreamed  up as a TV spin-off to another classic  Lynch story following the smash success  of his Prime Time Abc Thriller Twin  Peaks Lynch and co-creator Mark Frost  were preparing a second series centered  on the character Audrey home which was  to be named after a famous street in Los  Angeles where Frost lived in the book  conversations with Mark Frost the series  co-creator talked about how the movie  evolved from a TV pilot script to a  feature-length big screen success he  wrote we had considered spinning off the  Audrey character and setting her loose  in Hollywood in a modern Noir we had  very preliminary talks it drifted away  and then six years later I hear it's  going to be a pilot at ABC but when ABC  passed on the project 